      "a": "<p><em>A: <code>BaseException</code> is the common ancestor of all exception objects in CPython. Its direct subclasses include system exit signals: <code>KeyboardInterrupt</code> (SIGINT / Ctrl+C), <code>SystemExit</code> (emitted by <code>sys.exit()</code> and SIGTERM container signals), and <code>GeneratorExit</code>. <code>Exception</code> inherits from <code>BaseException</code> and serves as the root for all user/application-level errors. A bare <code>except:</code> catches <code>BaseException</code>, trapping <code>SystemExit</code>. When Kubernetes issues a SIGTERM to stop a container pod, a bare except catches it and refuses to terminate, causing the pod to hang until forcibly SIGKILLed after the grace period.</em></p>"
